  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Monday)\nIssued at 1214 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nThe western periphery of surface high pressure looks to hold over\na portion of the CWA into Wednesday. At the same time broad \nmid/upper level ridge of high pressure expands eastward into the \nsouthern Plains, and then flattens out for the second half of the\nweek. Underneath mid/upper high pressure, low level winds still \nlook to remain generally light, though more out of a southerly to \neasterly direction into the weekend. Temperatures should respond\nwith afternoon high temperatures above the seasonal average\nthrough the end of the forecast period. \n\nModel solutions continue to differ late weekend with a disturbance\ncurrently in the southwest portion of the Gulf progged to lift\nnorth/northeast. However, latest trends have been to keep this \ndisturbance east of the CWA. Thus, will continue PoPs below\nmentionable criteria late weekend and continue to monitor data\nthrough the week. In other words, no significant rainfall is\nforecast for the next 7 days.",
